<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE score-partwise PUBLIC "-//Recordare//DTD MusicXML 3.1 Partwise//EN"
  "http://www.musicxml.org/dtds/partwise.dtd">
<!-- Architectural Layer 3 reach-back fixture (cowork_layer3_reachback_design.md,
     Phase 3). 0 fifths, declared A minor (mode minor). Two halves:
       Bars 1-6  — an UNAMBIGUOUS C major establishment (I IV V I V I): the G-B-D
                   dominants carry the B leading tone (and there is no G#), so the
                   whole-sequence decode reads C major confidently across the head
                   despite the weak declared-minor hint.
       Bars 7-9  — a relative-pair tail (A minor / E minor / A minor — the exact
                   white-key content of s1c_a_minor_amb).
     Selecting ONLY bar 7 (a single A-minor triad) opens with a LOW-confidence A
     minor reading (the bare triad reads as its own tonic, but only weakly — the
     relative C major is close). Reach-back extends earlier into the C-major head,
     whose established key anchors the opening to C major (vi): the change cost is
     not repaid by a single Am measure. iso A-minor vs reached/whole C-major is the
     gap reach-back closes. Whole-note root-position triads keep each local fit clean. -->
